# Built by build_exe.bat
build/
dist/
*.spec.bak

# Runtime state - the catalogue, the cover cache, whatever the user has rated -
# lives in %LOCALAPPDATA%\slgking, not here, so there is normally nothing to
# ignore. Kept as a net for the case where slg_db.app_dir() ever falls back to
# the source tree: that file is personal and must never be committed.
data/
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# Promo film. tools/make_promo.py and tools/shot_dialogs.py are tracked; the
# frames they render are build output - the mp4 alone is megabytes of dead
# weight in git, and every shot in it is reproducible from the script.
promo/

# Throwaway
*.log
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Machine-local tooling. .claude/ is this machine's session memory and
# settings, .codepilot-uploads/ is screenshots pasted into chat, and the
# *.ai.md files are generated directory listings. None of it is source.
.claude/
.codepilot-uploads/
README.ai.md
PATH.ai.md

# Server side. The client talks to the author's server, but the deploy tool,
# the sync server and the catalogue host are single-tenant ops scripts -
# deploy_server.py alone names the host, the SSH port, the login user and the
# remote layout. They stay off the public repo. test_serve_catalog.py imports
# serve_catalog at module level, so it follows them out.
deploy_server.py
slg_sync_server.py
serve_catalog.py
tests/test_serve_catalog.py
